  "notes": "So So Def male quartet carrying Dupri and Bryan-Michael Cox's keyboard-ballad grammar, 1998–2004. The research bolds \"55–65 half-time (reads 110–130)\" as the spine with a 96–110 straight tail, so the felt band is the base with `halfTime` true and the snare on beat 3. Three drum deltas quote Cox's kit directly: \"kick on 1 and the 8th before 3\" at one or two hits a bar with syncopation at 0.1, \"clap+snare stacked on beat 3\", and \"16th hats only in the chorus\" — a non-continuous lane at 0.16 fill density; the entry's \"TR-808-styled kick/hat pair as the whole percussion bed\" is why the perc lanes collapse to a single snap at −11 dB. The identifying parameter is harmonic: \"rich extended chords (maj7, m7, add9) and a full 4–6 chord loop rather than a 2-chord vamp — Cox's harmonic vocabulary is the widest on the So So Def board\", so `maxChords` is 6, the top-weighted family is a six-chord cycle, the triad share falls to 0.12 and ninth rises to 0.38. \"Four-part harmony with the lead doubling in the octave\" is the counter at −12 with `octave_echo` leading. The low end is \"808-derived sub on chord roots with a slide into the downbeat; deliberately soft relative to the piano\" — a bass part on chord roots with a real glide, so no `drums.bass808` block. ⚠ The INFERRED parameters are all velocity and density numbers and `swing.amount` 0.50; the research gives keys, tempos and a chord vocabulary, not a programmed kit.",
